# WHAT THE KNOWLEDGE GRAPH MAY READ, AND THE ONE CATEGORY IT MAY NOT.
#
# graphify ingests every markdown file as a `document` and makes one node per heading. That is right
# for a specification, a handover or an operating manual: those describe the system, and a question
# about the system should find them.
#
# It is WRONG for an audit verdict. An audit says whether a build passed on one day against one
# standard. Its headings — "Verdicts", "Gate 8 — the inventory reconciles", "PHASE_D_NOT_READY" —
# read in a graph query exactly like statements about the estate, and they are statements about a
# past judgement of it. Measured on 25 Aug 2026 before this file existed: 274 heading nodes from 14
# audit documents, including a node literally labelled "Verdicts"
# (id `phase_c_final_acceptance_audit_verdicts`, from PHASE_C_FINAL_ACCEPTANCE_AUDIT.md L297). A
# later reader asking the graph what the estate does would have been answered, in part, by what an
# audit concluded about it in August.
#
# THE RULE IS A PATTERN, NOT A LIST, so it holds for audits nobody has written yet. Every entry below
# matches a FILENAME FAMILY, and each is named with what distinguishes it.
#
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY NOT EXCLUDED, so this is not a keep-list that quietly grew:
#   · *_ACCEPTANCE_CHECKLIST.md      — package INPUTS. They state what must be true, which is a
#                                      specification. Three of them are ingested and they stay.
#   · PHASE_*_RESULT.*               — result files record measurements, not verdicts. The Phase A-D
#                                      documentation that held them was deleted on 9 Sep 2026; the
#                                      pattern stays because it is a rule, not a list.
#   · docs/sessions/*                — handovers and briefs. They describe work, not judgements.
#     (the single exception below is named individually and says why)
#
# VERIFY THIS FILE RATHER THAN TRUST IT:
#   node -e "const g=require('./graphify-out/graph.json');
#            const AUD=/(INDEPENDENT_ACCEPTANCE|ACCEPTANCE_AUDIT|_AUDIT\.md$|FINAL_GATE_RESULTS|FINAL_.*CANARY|^audit\/)/i;
#            console.log(g.nodes.filter(n=>n.file_type==='document'&&AUD.test(n.source_file||'')).length)"
#   → must print 0 after a regeneration.

# ---- audit verdicts -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The independent acceptance audits. One per session, at the repository root and under docs/.
PHASE_*_FINAL_INDEPENDENT_ACCEPTANCE*.md
**/PHASE_*_FINAL_INDEPENDENT_ACCEPTANCE*.md

# The acceptance and re-acceptance audits.
**/*_ACCEPTANCE_AUDIT*.md
**/*_REACCEPTANCE_AUDIT*.md

# Anything whose name ENDS in _AUDIT.md is a judgement of the build by construction.
**/*_AUDIT.md

# The final canaries, trace results and remediation results: each is a verdict on one gate.
PHASE_*_FINAL_*CANARY*.md
PHASE_*_FINAL_TRACE_RESULT*.md
PHASE_*_FINAL_ZERO_COST_RESULT*.md
PHASE_*_REMEDIATION_RESULT*.md
PHASE_*_FINAL_GATE_RESULTS*.csv
PHASE_*_TEST_FAILURE_CLASSIFICATION*.csv

# The audit working directory.
audit/

# ---- the one individually named exclusion, and why ----------------------------------------------
# A word-by-word audit OF a session brief. It is a judgement, not a description, and its 14 heading
# nodes read as statements about the brief's subject rather than about the brief.
docs/sessions/NEXT_SESSION_BRIEF_WORD_BY_WORD_AUDIT.md

# ---- graphify's own output ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# A graph that ingests its own last report grows a second, fainter copy of itself every run.
graphify-out/
